      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To complete the task, I need to create the specified Python files with the required AWS integrations. The scored implementation files must use AWS services to perform the specified tasks. The local helper files will provide configuration and utility functions to support the scored files. Here's the plan:\n\n1. Create `detect_image_labels.py` to detect labels in an image using AWS Rekognition.\n2. Create `describe_image.py` to generate a visual description for an image using AWS Rekognition.\n3. Create `detect_image_text.py` to detect text in an image using AWS Rekognition.\n4. Create `score_image_safety.py` to check an image for unsafe content using AWS Rekognition.\n5. Create `vision_client.py` to provide configuration and client utilities for AWS Rekognition.\n6. Create `vision_models.py` to define request, response, and normalization helpers for AWS Rekognition.\n7. Create `image_summary.py` to summarize visual analysis results.\n8. Create `alt_text_translate.py` to translate generated image descriptions.\n9. Create `visual_safety_text.py` to check generated visual labels for unsafe text.\n10. Create `image_asset_archive.py` to archive image-analysis artifacts and derived captions in managed object storage.\n\nI will start by creating the `detect_image_labels.py` file. </thinking>\n\n",
