      "data": {
        "text": "All specified Python files have been created successfully in the current working directory.\n\nHere are the files and their purposes:\n1. **[SAME-SCENARIO] detect_image_labels.py** - Detects labels or objects in a static image using AWS Rekognition.\n2. **[SAME-SCENARIO] describe_image.py** - Generates a short visual description for an image using AWS Rekognition.\n3. **[SAME-SCENARIO] detect_image_text.py** - Detects text appearing inside an image using AWS Rekognition.\n4. **[SAME-SCENARIO] score_image_safety.py** - Checks an image for unsafe or policy-sensitive visual content using AWS Rekognition.\n5. **[HELPER] vision_client.py** - Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for AWS Rekognition.\n6. **[HELPER] vision_models.py** - Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for AWS Rekognition.\n7. **[LATER-STEP] image_summary.py** - Summarizes visual analysis results.\n8. **[LATER-STEP] alt_text_translate.py** - Translates generated image descriptions.\n9. **[LATER-STEP] visual_safety_text.py** - Checks generated visual labels for unsafe text.\n10. **[LATER-STEP] image_asset_archive.py** - Archives image-analysis artifacts and derived captions in managed object storage using AWS S3.\n\nEach scored implementation file uses AWS services to perform the specified tasks, and the local helper files provide configuration and utility functions to support the scored files.",
